. ../../testutils.sh

# What the code generator checks of the runtime contract: a routine the
# runtime has must have a flat form of its port's registers, whichever
# routines the program calls, a check whose evidence the lowering takes,
# and a foreign function the runtime implements must agree with `base`'s
# declaration; and of the static objects the lowering is given: one that
# holds another must hold one the program has. What does not stops the
# compile, with the reason. It uses the code generator's modules,
# installed as the package `idris2-native`.
idris2 -p idris2-native -p idris2 Gen.idr -o gen > /dev/null
./build/exec/gen
